    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country E.164 national-number length validation in the owner-creation flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\nThe `toE164(...)` normalizer (called from `normalizeNewOwner`, whose `false` return maps to `400 Bad Request` in `addOwner`) now rejects a number whose national-number length is wrong for its country code, via a new helper `nationalNumberLengthValid`:\n\n- `+61` (Australia) \u2014 requires exactly **9** national digits (digits after the `61` country code)\n- `+1` (NANP) \u2014 requires exactly **10** national digits (digits after the `1` country code)\n- Other country codes keep the pre-existing generic 8\u201315 total-digit rule.\n\nFor the test case `\"+61 123\"`, the cleaned digits `61123` yield 3 national digits, so the request is rejected with 400. Valid payloads still pass: the fixture `04XXXXXXXX` normalizes to `+61` with 9 national digits, and seeded `+1` NANP numbers carry 10.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` passes and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
